hat's exactly what I expected! g1=N \u2713, g2=b \u2713, g3=M \u2713, g4=Y \u2713.\nHmm, but G's target was g1=M, g2=Y, g3=N, g4=b. I messed up: G's target is green row R\u2192L = b, N, Y, M, i.e., g4=b, g3=N, g2=Y, g1=M.\nWhat I actually set up was: g1=N, g2=b, g3=M, g4=Y \u2014 this is green row L\u2192R = N, b, M, Y. That's not G!\nLet me recompute: G = (r1,r2,r4,g4,g3,g2,g1) = (O,p,R,b,N,Y,M) \u2192 g4=b, g3=N, g2=Y, g1=M.\nWhat I did: swap g1\u2194g4: g1 gets N (from g4), g4 gets Y. Swap g2\u2194g3: g2 gets b, g3 gets M. Result: g1=N, g2=b, g3=M, g4=Y.\nFor G I need g1=M, g2=Y, g3=N, g4=b. So I set up the wrong configuration \u2014 I confused myself. The current configuration (g1=N, g2=b, g3=M, g4=Y) is actually... green row L\u2192R = N,b,M,Y. As a hypothesis: red row L\u2192R (O,p,R), green row L\u2192R (N,b,M,Y)? That's not a simple frame order (frames 4-7 = b,N,Y,M; N,b,M,Y is a permutation of those).\nAnd SPACE was rejected (level_completed False).\nOK, so let me properly set up G: from current (g1=N, g2=b, g3=M, g4=Y), target (g1=M, g2=Y, g3=N, g4=b):\n- g1: N\u2192M, g2: b\u2192Y, g3: M\u2192N, g4: Y\u2192b.\nCycle: g1\u2192g3 (N\u2192M? no). Let me track the pieces: M is at g3, needs to go to g1. Y is at g4, needs to go to g2. N is at g1, needs to go to g3. b is at g2, needs to go to g4.\nCycle: g1\u2192g3\u2192g1? N: g1\u2192g3. M: g3\u2192g1. That's a 2-cycle (g1 g3). Y: g4\u2192g2. b: g2\u2192g4. 2-cycle (g2 g4).\nSo swap (g1,g3) and (g2,g4): 4 clicks + SPACE.\nIf G fails, next candidates:\n- G' (counterclockwise): r1=O, g1=p, g2=R, g3=b, g4=N, r4=Y, r2=M.\n- H3: r4=O, r2=p, r1=R, g1=b, g2=N, g3=Y, g4=M.\n- H4: r4=O, r2=p, r1=R, g4=b, g3=N, g2=Y, g1=M.\n- B: green row first.\nLet me test G now.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "I set the wrong config (my swaps gave N,b,M,Y not G's M,Y,N,b). Correcting to true G: swap (g1,g3) and (g2,g4), then SPACE.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL